  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Eliminating Lymphatic Filariasis (up to 10 African countries) ELFA - as part of Reaching the Last Mile Initiative.  New version.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ELFA programme will be implemented in partnership  with Sightsavers, as part of the Reaching the Last Mile Fund (RLMF) 2.0 &apos;Africa Free Initiative&apos;, the  aim of which is to eliminate two NTDs across Africa by 2030. The proposed FCDO funded activities, countries and focus on LF will align with FCDO&#x2019;s previous programme: Accelerating the Sustainability Control and Elimination of Neglected Tropical Diseases (ASCEND) to tackle the disease.  This decision will continue the important work achieved under our previous programme in helping to deliver towards the SDGs. (SDG 3.3 By 2030, end the epidemics of AIDS, tuberculosis, malaria and neglected tropical diseases and combat hepatitis, water-borne diseases and other communicable diseases.)  RLMF is managed by Gates and would be implemented by three major partners: Sightsavers, The Carter Fund and the End Fund and will complement other large NTD programmes (those of WHO &amp; USAID).</narrative>
  </description>
